From 8b0777533860b2a7f4f774c43bf5303ec0a2bb52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:29:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 34/34] wsi: VK_KHR_display on the PS4's VideoOut

The PS5's VideoOut WSI (wsi_common_videoout.c) presents on the PS4 too,
with MESA_WSI_VIDEOOUT_PS4 selecting the PS4's calls:

- one display and one 1920x1080 mode at 59.94 Hz, no high-frame-rate one;
- five 16 MiB framebuffers of garlic direct memory, imported into the
  device as host memory, B8G8R8A8 (VideoOut's A8R8G8B8);
- registered with sceVideoOutRegisterBuffers once the first swapchain's
  images are laid out in them, in VideoOut's tiled mode at the images'
  pitch: RADV gives a GFX7 scanout image the 2D thin display tiling that
  mode scans out, the layout freegnm computes for a display surface
  (tile mode 10, pitch 1920, 1920x1088, 32 KiB aligned);
- flipped with sceVideoOutSubmitFlip at a vblank, the shown flip read
  from sceVideoOutGetFlipStatus, acquires waiting with
  sceVideoOutWaitVblank, as on the PS5.

The PS4 build links libSceVideoOut, and its host model runs the same
swapchain logic with stand-ins for the calls.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KvB274h9yAsuA8U9fnRoFR
